Every collision/trigger needs 3 things:

1️⃣ A Collider
2️⃣ A Rigidbody
3️⃣ A Script to detect events

If any ONE is missing → collision/trigger will not work.
✅ Golden Rule 1: At least ONE object must have a Rigidbody

Otherwise OnTriggerEnter / OnCollisionEnter will NEVER fire.

Examples:

Player (Rigidbody + Collider)

Enemy (Collider only)

Coin (Collider marked as Trigger)

This works because Player has Rigidbody.
✅ Golden Rule 3: Script can be placed on EITHER object
BUT whichever object has the script → that object receives the event.

How to get Trigger Point (Easy Trick)
✔️ Use Collider.ClosestPoint():

void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other)
{
    Vector3 pointA = GetComponent<Collider>().ClosestPoint(other.transform.position);
    Vector3 pointB = other.ClosestPoint(transform.position);

    Vector3 triggerPoint = (pointA + pointB) / 2f;

    Debug.Log("Approx Trigger Point: " + triggerPoint);
}

🟥 2. Collision (OnCollisionEnter) → YES, gives exact contact point
void OnCollisionEnter(Collision collision)
{
    foreach (ContactPoint contact in collision.contacts)
    {
        Debug.Log("Collision Point: " + contact.point);
    }
}

